Q: How can we resolve Gemini API block_reason: OTHER when using Gemini 3 Pro Image Preview for sensitive entities? A: <h1>Use a custom <code>fetch</code> agent in Node.js to route requests through a OXYLABS DATACENTER US Proxy.</h1>
<p><strong>We</strong> found that the <code>block_reason: OTHER</code> is frequently triggered by localized compliance filters in the EU. To bypass this, <strong>we</strong> routed <strong>our</strong> requests through <strong>Oxylabs US Datacenter Proxies</strong>. You also can get datacenter proxies free from OXYLABs.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/bZqfkdnU.png" alt="oxylab dashboard" title="datacenter proxy" /></p>
<p>In Node.js, the <code>@google/genai</code> SDK allows you to provide a custom <code>fetch</code> implementation. <strong>We</strong> used the <code>https-proxy-agent</code> library to ensure the API sees the request as originating from the US.</p>
<h3><strong>Our Solution: Custom Proxy Agent</strong></h3>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>Install the proxy agent:</strong></p>
<p>Bash</p>
<pre><code>npm install https-proxy-agent

</code></pre>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Configure the client with a custom fetch:</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>JavaScript</p>
<pre><code>import { GoogleGenAI } from &quot;@google/genai&quot;;
import { HttpsProxyAgent } from &quot;https-proxy-agent&quot;;
import fetch from &quot;node-fetch&quot;; // Or use native fetch in Node 18+

// Our US Proxy credentials
const proxyUrl = &quot;http://user:pass@us-area.proxies.oxylabs.io:12345&quot;;
const proxyAgent = new HttpsProxyAgent(proxyUrl);

// We create a custom fetch wrapper that uses the proxy agent
const proxiedFetch = (url, options) =&gt; {
  return fetch(url, { ...options, agent: proxyAgent });
};

const genAI = new GoogleGenAI(&quot;YOUR_API_KEY&quot;);

async function generateWithProxy() {
  // Pass the custom fetch to the model initialization
  const model = genAI.getGenerativeModel(
    { model: &quot;gemini-3-pro-image-preview&quot; },
    { fetch: proxiedFetch } 
  );

  const prompt = &quot;A detailed report on [Public Figure]'s latest tech venture.&quot;;

  // This previously triggered 'OTHER' for us in the EU
  const result = await model.generateContent(prompt);
  console.log(result.response.text());
}

generateWithProxy();
</code></pre>
<h3><strong>Why this worked for us:</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>IP-Based Filtering:</strong> The Gemini API applies different safety &quot;wrappers&quot; based on the source IP. By using a US-based proxy, <strong>we</strong> moved out of the stricter EU-specific blocklist.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Consistency:</strong> This method bypasses the <code>block_reason: OTHER</code> without needing to change <strong>our</strong> prompt structure or hosting region.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Result:</strong> After implementing the US proxy, <strong>our</strong> success rate for entity-sensitive prompts returned to 100%.</p>
